.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 13, 2026
.Dt FSCK 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm fsck
.Nd check and repair file systems
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl fnpy
.Op Fl t Ar type
.Op Ar special | node ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
checks file systems by running each type's own checker,
.Pa /sbin/fsck_ Ns Ar type
.Pq Xr fsck_oxfs 8 .
With no file systems named, it checks every entry of
.Xr fstab 5
with a nonzero pass number, lowest pass first.
A file system named is looked up in
.Xr fstab 5
by device or mount point; one not there is taken to be of the
.Fl t
type, oxfs by default.
.Pp
The options
.Fl f ,
.Fl n ,
.Fl p
and
.Fl y
are passed to the checkers; see
.Xr fsck_oxfs 8 .
.Pp
.Xr rc 8
runs
.Nm Fl p
at boot, while the root file system is still mounted read-only.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The worst status any checker returned: 0 when every file system is clean or
was repaired, 8 when one needs checking by hand.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr fstab 5 ,
.Xr fsck_oxfs 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr rc 8
